---
import SocialLinks from "../components/layout/SocialLinks.astro";
import { topics } from "../data/topics";
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
---

<PageLayout
  title="Hi, I’m Vidya"
  label="The person behind the period"
  description="I build software, systems, and occasionally problems that require software and systems to solve."
  ><div class="reading-column about-body prose">
    <p>
      I’ve spent the last several years working across backend engineering,
      cloud infrastructure, AI, startups, and engineering leadership.
    </p><p>
      This is where I write about what I’ve learned while building things. The
      useful patterns. The less useful assumptions. The decisions that looked
      perfectly reasonable before they met production.
    </p><h2>Publication first. Portfolio second.</h2><p>
      Good engineering writing makes the reasoning visible. What did we know?
      What did we trade away? What would we do differently?
    </p><p>
      That’s the kind of space I want this to be: serious about the work,
      comfortable with uncertainty, and willing to laugh at a questionable
      decision.
    </p><h2>Things I keep coming back to</h2><dl class="interests">
      {
        topics.map(({ slug, title, description, href }) => (
          <div id={`topic-${slug}`}>
            <dt>{href ? <a href={href}>{title}</a> : title}</dt>
            <dd>{description}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl><p>
      If that sounds like your kind of reading, <a href="/writing/"
        >start with the writing</a
      >.
    </p><h2>Elsewhere on the internet</h2><SocialLinks
      label="Find Vidya and follow the publication"
    />
  </div></PageLayout
>

<style>
  .interests {
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
  }
  .interests > div {
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .interests dt {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .interests dd {
    margin: 0.15rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
